A hidden, experimental `--member-invariants` option, requiring `--type-system-refresh`, begins member invariants (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/105). In this first stage, a datatype, class, trait, newtype or abstract type may declare `invariant e` members; they are parsed, printed and resolved as ghost predicates of the type, with the plan's reads restriction (an invariant depends on no mutable state); an invariant is never opaque. The verifier reports invariants as not yet supported, and compiled code ignores them. A codatatype may not declare an invariant, and a program, libraries included, that declares a member invariant may not declare a codatatype. `witness` members and `raw T` are parsed but not yet supported. A `.doo` library built with the option requires it of its clients; one built without it is unchanged. Without the option, parsing, diagnostics and the generated Boogie are unchanged.
